# cursorrules.md

## Module Documentation Rules

### Structure

- Begin with a short overview of what this module covers.
- Divide content into sections: Introduction, Concepts, Setup, Usage, Examples, and Troubleshooting (if relevant).
- Each sub-section should be in a separate file and referenced via `SUMMARY.md`.

### Content Expectations

- Provide diagrams or flowcharts using `mermaid` if applicable.
- Include a real-world use-case or scenario.
- Clearly mention any pre-requisites or dependencies.

### Code Samples

- Ensure samples are syntactically correct and runnable if copied.
- Include `Expected Output` if relevant.
- Prefer minimal examples that focus on core concepts.

### Update Policy

- Revisit this module’s docs whenever the code changes significantly.
- Deprecate outdated sections with clear notes, e.g., `> Deprecated since v1.2`.

### Review Checklist

- [ ] All sections have headings.
- [ ] Syntax and spell-check completed.
- [ ] All internal links resolve correctly.
- [ ] Tested with `mdbook build`.

